To count distinct subsequences, we can use dynamic programming. Let dp[i][j] be the number of distinct subsequences of the first i characters of S ending with the j-th character. Then, dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j] + dp[i-1][j-1] if S[i-1] == j, and dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j] otherwise. The answer is the sum of dp[n][j] for all j. Since the result may be large, we return the answer modulo 10^9 + 7.
